.TH FREE 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
free \- display the amount of memory in use and free
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B free
.RB [ \-b | \-k | \-m | \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B free
prints the computer's memory: the total (the RAM installed), what is
in use, and what is free.
.PP
Before measuring it runs a full garbage collection 20 times, since
Lua's collector frees some objects (those with finalizers, for one)
only on a later cycle; so
.I used
is what is really held, not garbage waiting to be collected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-b
Show amounts in bytes.
.TP
.B \-k
Show amounts in KiB (the default).
.TP
.B \-m
Show amounts in MiB.
.TP
.B \-h
Show amounts in human\-readable form, with a unit after each:
.BR B ,
.BR Ki ,
.B Mi
or
.BR Gi .
.PP
Each option is a separate argument; the last unit given wins, and
.B \-h
wins over any unit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 for an unknown option or if the memory could not be
read.
.SH NOTES
There is no swap, so there is no
.B Swap:
line, and no buffer or cache columns.
The total is the RAM installed above what the firmware itself holds.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR ps (1)
